[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692127976","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103418#issuecomment-2692127976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103418","id":2692127976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gdpzo","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-01T10:27:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-01T10:27:21Z","body":"Problem with a script is you can only have one per node, every unique object type would require its unique script with lots of exported variables to allow custom behavior. With child nodes as components you can reuse and combine game logic in an artist-friendly way, a wider range of unique behaviors can be achieved for imported assets in editor without touching any code. One script approach is good for solo projects when everything is code, but won't scale that well to teams where programmers and game designers are separate people focused on solving different problems\r\n\r\n> This is a good use case for inherited scenes, and the editable children checkbox, but there are currently some issues with those\r\n\r\nWhy one script instead of improving those workflows? Not only inherited scenes / editable children allow components, they also allow adding and previewing unique node types like particle systems and connect signals in editor","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692127976/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692128582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103418#issuecomment-2692128582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103418","id":2692128582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gdp9G","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-01T10:28:55Z","updated_at":"2025-03-01T10:28:55Z","body":"Yes please I'm one of said advanced users :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"u